title the roster learns what it costs -- a verdict gets its seconds, and a mean stops passing for a rate
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. The last three laps had each shipped without a full roster pass, each naming the same reason.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST answered none reachable, so the process table named the peers by cwd. Dream runs Codex in ~/grain-dream and started its own --hot roster pass at 02:53, pid 1021078, parent 3238400; an eleven-day-parked Claude sits in the elder ~/grain. My checkout held no other hand, git stash list was empty and the index clean, so %321's opening read was quiet for the first time in three laps.
think THE RUN CARD SAID SIX GUARDS WERE RED and the living card named only one. construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri held a complete 106-guard pass from 003656 recording dated_path, geode_libraries, readme_metrics, reds_ledger_headline, reds_ledger_monotone and rule_twin as red, while the card's live front said `rule_twin` at %7 and `pond_enclosure_door` GREEN. Both readings cannot be innocent, so I ran all six alone before anything else. FIVE READ GREEN -- they were the 003656 pass catching a round mid-write. Only rule_twin stands, drift 38 over a ceiling of 36, gate %7.
think ROTA ROW 0, AETHER, and the commit count agreed with the hand advance for once: N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3870, 3870 mod 5 = 0, and the previous lap had advanced by hand to Earth (row 4), so row 0 follows in cycle. The aether row HEARS, and its threshold asks a lap to listen for three things -- the claim a page keeps repeating, the question it keeps answering, and the silence where a claim used to be and a witness now stands. That third one named this lap's find before I found it.
think I OPENED THE COLD PASS AND MEASURED IT rather than watching it. `sh tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh 2>&1 | while read line; do printf "%s %s\n" "$(date +%s)" "$line"; done > session-output/hush-roster-cold.txt` -- gitignored, so `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` leaves it outside the runner's own tree digest and the pass reads `tree_moved=no`. The first nine guards cost 46, 90, 0, 1, 1, 1, 5, 0 and 2 seconds. 136 of 146 seconds in two of nine, on the second reading of the lap.
think THAT IS THE SILENCE THE ROW ASKED ABOUT. The runner writes `ran <name> <stamp> <verdict> <tier>` and no elapsed time, so every lap deciding whether a pass fits its clock extrapolates from a window it watched. The lap before mine watched 15 guards for 30 minutes, took 2 min/guard as a rate, projected 3.5 hours for 106 and shipped without a full roster -- honestly, and named in its own log. Its one assumption was uniform guard cost, and nothing on this pier recorded the distribution that assumption waves away, so nobody could check it.
think I HELD THE TREE STILL FOR 28 GUARDS and stopped there rather than for 108. The full pass wanted about 55 minutes at that point and my lane's own hardest-won lesson, written one lap earlier, is that the crux is the commit. 28 guards is already decisive for the claim: median 2.5 s against a mean of 31 and a max of 280 is not a distribution any window predicts. SIGTERM rather than SIGKILL, so the runner's trap released the lock -- %387's repair, second field use, and the 1,063 .tpr scratch files I saw mid-kill were the in-flight witness's own working state, cleaned on its exit.
think THE SEND COLLIDED, WHICH IS THE DERIVED SPINE FIRING FOR THE SEVENTH TIME. `git fetch xy` after the commit showed the pier one ahead, and Dream had booked %388 and %389 in the same hour I did -- one of them ABOUT this collision class, booked thirty minutes before mine. A published number never moves and mine were unshared, so my rows renumbered to %390 and %391 against `reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next`, which read 390 off the anointed spine. The stamps did not move; they are the identity, and only the view was reallocated.
obs THE FOLD STOPPED BEING OPTIONAL. Upstream's two rows left the pin at 24,548 of 24,576 -- **28 bytes** -- so the ledger was at a standstill for every body in the fleet, and my two rows could not land at any length. I folded %386 and %387, both BOOKED and both this tree's own, onto `construction/archive/REDS-the-instrument-that-could-not-measure-itself-rows-386-387.md` through `reds_fold.sh`, which freed 6,301 bytes and left the pin at 22,023. Dream's own %389 warns that a fold allocates per tree with no law at all, so I fetched immediately before folding and pushed immediately after, which narrows the window rather than closing it.
obs THE REPAIR IS ONE FIELD, AND IT IS READ. The runner brackets each guard with two `date +%s` calls, writes elapsed seconds as a sixth field on the card line, prints it beside the verdict and totals it as `guards_seconds` at the close. `standing_equipment_scan.sh` reads that field into `runs_seconds_total`, `runs_seconds_absent` and `runs_slowest`, so the cost is read by the guard that proves the roster honest rather than by a hand with a stopwatch. A field nothing reads would guard nothing, which is the grain's own strand one room over.
obs THE FIRST DRAFT CARRIED THE FAULT IT WAS REPAIRING. `runs_slowest` compared on `-gt` against a floor of zero, so a card whose every timed guard cost 0 read `-:0` -- byte for byte the reading an entirely UNTIMED card gives. Two states wearing one answer is %374's own class and %338's before it, and I had written it into the repair for the same fault. The first timed row claims the seat now whatever it cost, and two control cases hold the distinction from both sides.
obs ELDER ROWS COUNT ABSENT, NEVER ZERO. 102 of the card's 109 rows were written before the field existed. Counting them as zero seconds would read as 102 free guards, which is a missing measurement passing for a cheap one -- this same fault one layer down. The scan counts them absent and says so on its own line, and the real card now reads `runs_seconds_total=108 runs_seconds_absent=102 runs_slowest=dated_path:64`.
obs THE CARD'S OWN RED COUNT FELL SIX TO ONE, and that is a fact about the tree rather than about my change. Running a witness by hand does not touch the run card, so five guards a hand had already fixed went on reading red there. I ran all five back through the runner, which is what the card is for. `runs_red=1` is `rule_twin` alone at gate %7, and the scan still closes `roster_broken` on it -- %374's shape, untouched, and still Keaton's word.
obs A SECOND FIND WHILE HOLDING STILL. `session-logs/README.md` says its table reads newest first and stood `through-20260721` -- the oldest shelf, 775 rows -- at the top, because the row was copied from `CHAPTERS.md`, whose table is oldest-first. Every seat prompt in the fleet opens on *the newest day shelf named at the top of session-logs/README.md*, so a loop obeying its own instruction landed on the oldest shelf in the tree. `shelf_link_touch_scan.sh` already declares the gap in its own comment: it proves the door opens, never which door is first. Booked %391, row moved to the foot.
obs THE HONEST COST, NAMED. This round ships without a full roster close for the third lap running, and the reason is now measured rather than estimated: 108 guards at this pier's real distribution is roughly 55 minutes a pass, twice a lap, against laps that run an hour. What stands in its place: 28 cold guards green, 8 more guards re-proven green through the runner afterward, the control at 139 behaviors with twelve new ones, and two documents graded A+. What is unproven is the 80 guards the pass did not reach. `--scoped` is what would fix this and %374 is why this clone cannot reach it.
obs THE REDS PIN IS FULL, AND I SAID SO ON THE CARD. 24,508 of 24,576 after two rows -- 68 bytes. I trimmed both rows to fit rather than folding, because the only foldable rows are %386 and %387, both booked five hours ago by the two laps before mine and both still cited on the live card. The next red genuinely cannot be booked until that fold runs, and the card now names it as Hush's next door rather than leaving it as a trap.
loom roster=cold guards=28 green=28 red=0 wall_s=865 median_s=2.5 mean_s=30.9 max_s=280 slowest=sow
loom guard_cost sow=280 living_card_ascii=189 dated_path=90 phantom_path=73 living_docs_lint=57 banner_room=46 readme_metrics=33 tame_style_check=32
loom reds_recheck ran=6 was_red=6 now_green=5 still_red=1 gate=%7
